you know the other guys  are being serious  they're not leaking this they are  behaving properly and vice versa and  then the way it worked because it was  such a long and difficult negotiation  you know the agenda had six points and  so you after the first six months of we  first did the the framework agreement  that took about six months then we  started work on the first point of the  framework agreement which was the issue  of rural development and after about six  months we reached our first agreement  and then another six months we reached  another agreement on the issue of  political participation and so forth in  what I call an incremental strategy so  that the more results you achieved the  heart it was for either side to think  that they were going to pull out of this  or they had no trust because they could  see they were ready to commit it to the  process now it didn't mean that it was  guaranteed you were going to get a  result there were some issues  particularly this justice issue where  things could have collapsed or this  issue of political participation I've  been alluding to but on the whole I  think as a friend of mine you knew a lot  about these things told me  before we even engaged the FARC what you  actually trust is not so much the person  by the process you need if the process  works well then each both sides have  trust in the process so I know there are  more questions but we're out of time  just before bringing those machetes to  it and just to remind everybody there  will be a reception upstairs to  immediately fall into which everyone is  invited  [Applause]  [Music]
 

